============================================================
  Paley Tournament P_13
============================================================
  WARNING: p = 13 ≡ 1 (mod 4), not 3 (mod 4).
  Paley tournament requires p ≡ 3 (mod 4).
  For p ≡ 1 (mod 4), -1 is a QR, so the 'tournament' is
  actually a self-complementary graph (not a tournament).
  We'll construct the QR-directed digraph anyway.

  Quadratic residues mod 13: [1, 3, 4, 9, 10, 12]
  |QR| = 6 = (p-1)/2 = 6
  Is tournament: False
  Score sequence: [6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6]
  Regular: True (all scores = 6)

  Parity-check matrix H = A (mod 2):
    Size: 13 x 13
    GF(2) rank: 12
    Code length n = 13
    Code dimension k = 13 - 12 = 1
    Null space dimension: 1
    Null space verified: all basis vectors satisfy Hx=0
    Computing minimum distance (brute force over 2 codewords)...
    Minimum distance d = 13  (exact, brute force)
    Time: 0.00s

    Weight distribution:
      w=  0: 1 codewords
      w= 13: 1 codewords

  => Code parameters: [13, 1, 13]

  Self-orthogonality check (H * H^T mod 2):
    Diagonal values mod 2: {0}
    Off-diagonal values mod 2: {0, 1}
    H * H^T = 0 (mod 2): False

